Subject: Chainsaw: do not hold the equipment because its 3 damage would kill nothing
Why: Same refusal as Nova Hellkite (0009): AiController.checkETBEffects asks DamageDealAi
  whether it would use the ETB, and with no opposing creature that 3 damage kills the answer
  is no, so the AI kept Chainsaw in hand (Boros Dwarves, patched round robin: castable but
  never cast in 25 of the 38 games where it could have been cast). The trigger already says
  "up to one target", so OptionalDecider$ You changes nothing in the rules: declining is the
  same as choosing no target. The AI now plays Chainsaw as an equipment and still shoots a
  creature when the damage kills it.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/boros-dwarves.txt --vs <the other ten meta decks> -n 100
  --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e with patches 0001-0008, on 14 Nov 2026. Without:
  74.5% (95% CI 72-77%, 745-255). With this patch: 74.4% (72-77%, 744-256). Difference -0.1
  points, 95% CI -3.9 to +3.7 (paired over the same 1,000 seeds: -1.6 to +1.4): no effect on
  the win rate. Chainsaw cast in 408 of the 444 games where it was seen (284 of 444 without).
  Mirror with 0009 and 0010 (`match boros-dwarves boros-dwarves -n 200 --seed 1`): 48.0%
  (41-55%).

